From 9ad680ea01b5b513174d44b6c01868eaa4623d12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 06:40:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v2): build the Korea conversion-curve artifact from
 filed pairs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Contract Check is not unbuilt, it is starved: buildContractCheckRouteModel
reads SIGNEDPRICE_CONVERSION_CURVE_ARTIFACT/_PERIOD/_SHA256 and degrades the
whole screen to "Comparison paused" when the artifact is absent. Production
build logs confirm [signedprice:conversion-curve] artifact_missing. Nothing in
the repository could produce that artifact: the published summaries carry
depositWon only, because the fixed filter is zero-rent jeonse, which excludes
exactly the rent-bearing contracts a conversion rate is measured between.

Adds the missing pipeline. A pair is same building x same filed area x two
deposits, and the rate is read at the LOWER deposit, the one written on the
contract carrying the rent. Anchors are band medians of implied rates over
observed deposits, never band edges.

The refusals are the point. A band under minimumPairsPerAnchor is dropped
rather than published with a wider error bar; a curve left with fewer than two
anchors is omitted rather than extrapolated; a missing required curve fails the
run rather than writing a half artifact that deploys cleanly and still shows a
paused screen; a collector checkpoint carrying holes is refused outright. The
artifact is parsed with the site's own parseKoreaConversionArtifact before it
is written, so anything on disk is something the deployment accepts.

The sha256 is over the source extract bytes, sealing which extract produced
these anchors.

Tests: 17 new (9 pairing, 8 runner), including the 만원 to 원 factor and the
exact eligiblePairCount the parser recomputes. Full suite 1139 passed,
typecheck clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
